{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791818826,"nonce":"GjCWZRl0/HPonwwzk6NQRkL1UF4=","title":"Track the agreed compiler optimization effort: reduce cumulative allocated bytes through generic interprocedural producer-consumer fusion (deforestation). This is a plan, not an implemented optimization or a promised speedup.","message":"Fixed contract:\n- Keep BenchBinaryTrees.hx and bench_binary_trees.hl unchanged, including depth 16, iteration counts, and checksum -104864. No benchmark-name recognition, hardcoded algebra/checksum, or reduced workload.\n- Hybrid is the primary acceptance configuration. AOT helps distinguish optimization quality from tier promotion timing; AOT-only success is insufficient.\n- Preserve observable semantics under an explicitly documented allocation-elimination contract. Unknown legality means retain the original program.\n- Measure actual cumulative allocation. Moving storage to arenas or excluding it from accounting is not allocation elimination.\n- Commit each completed implementation checkpoint and append commit IDs, validation evidence, and remaining limitations to the corresponding issue.\n\nEvidence and proposed scope:\nThe source implies roughly 29.6 million constructed nodes; roughly 32 bytes per node is consistent with the reported 900.1 MiB cumulative allocation. Reconcile the precise difference before treating the counter as exact. Local SROA removes some allocations exposed by inlining, but recursive child returns and stores are real interprocedural escape boundaries. More inlining alone does not solve arbitrary recursive depth.\nInitial target: a fresh recursive tree immediately consumed by a read-only recursive scalar calculation, as in bottomUpTree(item, depth).itemCheck(). Derive the fused helper from IR. Initially retain the long-lived tree, whose construction and use straddle the main loop.\n\nPublished baseline reference: https://github.com/rayzor-blade/ash/actions/runs/38246817230/job/114806786783 at source d74540baf79d85c6d8ee8092db0b3fd7f7086bab. Hybrid checksum -104864, reported 900.1 MiB allocation; timing and GC instrumentation are separate runs. Older sweeps used different CPUs, so published timing differences are not causal evidence. New claims require interleaved old/new runs on the same CI host.\n\nSeven checkpoints: baseline; candidate legality analysis; generated recursive helper infrastructure; fusion; differential/backend correctness; allocation and performance measurements; bounded default rollout. Child IDs and dependencies are recorded in a follow-up comment.\n\nRelated existing issues: 1c26b13 (local SROA limitations) and 7e9d728 (TLAB statistics hide small allocations). Reuse their work where applicable; recursive fusion is a separate scope.\nPrimary code: crates/air/src/v2/module.rs, crates/air/src/v2/passes/sroa.rs, crates/air/src/v2/passes/inline.rs, crates/air/src/v2/passes/mod.rs, crates/ash/src/air_pipeline.rs, std/src/obj.rs, std/src/gc.rs; benchmark tooling scripts/ash_bench.py and bench/benchmarks.toml.","files":null}]}